cable standardized across a national footprint, from GYFS-864 and GCYFTY-432 down to 24-fiber counts.</p></div></div><div class="recent-projects-cta xtxikjs"><p class="xvuptk1">Building in your region? Send your specification for a quote.</p><a class="request-a-quote-button xr2ljj3" href="/contact-vocomai"><p class="xx8ete8">Request a Quote</p></a></div></section><section class="content-video xphg3xo"><h2 class="xlo36pu">See how Vocom sources your cable</h2><div class="video-frame xo2uzpf fb"><div class="video xskwkwe"><video class="video-fill" src="/assets/video/fiber-optic-cables-b335b5.mp4" autoplay loop playsinline controls preload="auto" style="object-fit:cover;border-radius:0px;"></video></div></div></section><div class="xbrpt6a"><p class="xyfvjmk">Two Ways to Get Fiber From Vocom</p><p class="xlffj3m">Every project has a different tolerance for lead time. Choose the program that fits your timeline.</p><div class="xvtkojt fb"><div class="x4tkegk"><div class="xpx3c8u"></div><div class="xpx3c8u"><p class="xehzbkn">Standard Program</p></div><div class="xpx3c8u"><p class="xehzbkn">Expedited Program</p></div></div><div class="xw5wegs"><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="xeuva4f">Lead Time</p></div><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="x95npfr">Standard: 6 to 8 weeks (production + ocean freight)</p></div><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="x95npfr xog3e4r">2 to 3 weeks (production + air freight)</p><p class="x95npfr x3lh22k">Expedited: 2 to 3 weeks (production + air freight)</p></div></div><div class="xmo3sy2"><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="xeuva4f">Best For</p></div><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="x95npfr xog3e4r">Planned, recurring, forecastable demand</p><p class="x95npfr x3lh22k">Standard: Planned, recurring, forecastable demand</p></div><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="x95npfr xog3e4r">Timeline-critical deployments with fixed deadlines</p><p class="x95npfr x3lh22k">Expedited: Timeline-critical deployments with fixed deadlines</p></div></div><div class="xw5wegs"><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="xeuva4f">Inventory</p></div><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="x95npfr xog3e4r">Build-to-order, no US stock</p><p class="x95npfr x3lh22k">Standard: Build-to-order, no US stock</p></div><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="x95npfr xog3e4r">Made-to-order, built to your spec</p><p class="x95npfr x3lh22k">Expedited: Made-to-order, built to your spec</p></div></div><div class="xmo3sy2"><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="xeuva4f">Pricing</p></div><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="x95npfr xog3e4r">Standard channel pricing</p><p class="x95npfr x3lh22k">Standard: Standard channel pricing</p></div><div class="xdbhhf9"><p class="x95npfr xog3e4r">Premium reflects faster production and air freight</p><p class="x95npfr x3lh22k">Expedited: Premium reflects faster production and air freight</p></div></div></div><p class="xco9t8h">Both programs draw on the same quality standards and specifications. Talk to your Vocom representative about which program fits your timeline.</p></div><div class="how-ordering-works xbrpt6a"><h2 class="xyfvjmk">How Ordering Works</h2><div class="ordering-steps xsevupm"><div class="step-1 xhzxyxw fb"><p class="xeb4wi7">1. Send project requirements</p><p class="xurex9d">Cable type, fiber count, length, timeline.</p></div><div class="step-2 xhzxyxw fb"><p class="xeb4wi7">2. Receive quote and production timeline</p><p class="xurex9d">Quote plus estimated lead time.</p></div><div class="step-3 xhzxyxw fb"><p class="xeb4wi7">3. Manufacturing and quality check</p><p class="xurex9d">Produced and quality-checked per order.</p></div><div class="step-4 xhzxyxw fb"><p class="xeb4wi7">4. International shipping and delivery</p><p class="xurex9d">Shipped worldwide with import/export support.</p></div></div><p class="xysyof5">Estimated lead time: 6 to 8 weeks standard, up to 10 weeks for custom or high-count orders.</p></div><div class="section-divider xoxls24"><div class="xhawjdc"></div><div class="xkuqrqs"></div><div class="xhawjdc"></div></div><div class="faq xckvkrd"><h2 class="xyfvjmk">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><p class="xtv2frl">We are here to clear your doubts:</p><div class="faq-list xgpa4cm"><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Do you supply internationally?">Yes. VOCOM supports global fiber optic cable import and export for telecommunications, infrastructure, and data center projects worldwide. Shipping timelines vary depending on destination and order volume.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Can you handle bulk and wholesale cable orders?">Yes. We specialize in bulk and wholesale fiber optic cable supply for large-scale infrastructure and telecom deployments, including custom project requirements.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Do you provide technical datasheets and specifications?">Yes. Technical datasheets and product specifications are available upon request for all standard fiber optic cable types and custom configurations.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="What does Vocom International supply?">Vocom International supplies fiber optic cable and connectivity solutions, founded in 1998 with a focus on cross-Pacific and Asia-Pacific routes. We specify, source and deliver cable built to your requirements.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Who manufactures the cable?">Cable is produced to specification by tier 1 manufacturing partners on Fujikura preform glass. Vocom handles specification, sourcing, build-to-order coordination and delivery.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="What is the typical lead time?">Standard build-to-order programs run 6 to 8 weeks, and up to 10 weeks for high-count or custom builds. Confirm the date against your actual specification when you request a quote.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Is there an expedited option?">Yes. An expedited program is available at 2 to 3 weeks, covering production and air freight.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Is there a minimum order quantity?">Order sizes depend on the construction and fiber count. Send us your specification and quantity and we will confirm any minimums with your quote.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Can you supply custom fiber counts and constructions?">Yes. Cable is built to order, so fiber count, construction and jacket can be specified to suit the route and the install method.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Which fiber type do I need: G.652D, G.657A1 or G.657A2?">G.652D is the standard for outside plant and long-distance routes. G.657A1 and G.657A2 are bend-insensitive types for drops and indoor work, with A2 handling tighter bends. If you are unsure, send us the route details and we will recommend one.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Should I choose aerial or buried cable?">It depends on span, terrain, make-ready cost and lead time. Aerial routes use self-supporting ADSS cable, while buried routes use armored direct burial or duct cable. Our blog guide on aerial versus buried outside plant fiber walks through the trade-offs.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="What is rollable ribbon fiber and when is it used?">Rollable ribbon bonds fibers at intervals so the ribbon folds into a compact cylinder. It carries higher counts in a given duct than flat ribbon, and still supports mass fusion splicing. It is typically used for ultra-high-count data center and long-haul builds.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="What is mass fusion splicing?">Mass fusion splicing joins a whole 12-fiber ribbon in one operation instead of one fiber at a time. On high-count cable this cuts splicing labor sharply, which is why ribbon constructions are common above a few hundred fibers.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Do you supply connectors and hardware?">Yes. The catalog covers connectors and hardware alongside cable, including factory-terminated MTP/MPO trunks and break-out harnesses for data center builds.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Which fiber counts do you supply for data centers?">Data center builds typically range from hundreds of fibers at the edge to 864 and 1,728 in colocation and cloud, and higher counts for hyperscale. Ribbon and rollable ribbon constructions are available for the highest counts.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="What test data and certifications are available?">Datasheets and test data are available on request. Tell us the standards your project requires and we will confirm what applies to your specification.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="What delivery terms do you offer?">Delivery terms such as FOB or DDP can be quoted depending on the destination. Include the delivery location in your request and we will confirm.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="How do I request a quote, and what should I include?">Use the contact page and include the cable type, fiber count, quantity, route or install method and delivery location. The more complete the specification, the faster we can confirm price and lead time.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="What is fiber optic cable?">Fiber optic cable carries data as pulses of light through thin glass strands instead of electrical signals through copper. It supports far higher bandwidth and longer distances without signal loss, which is why it is the standard for telecommunications, data centers, and internet backbone infrastructure.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="What is single mode fiber cable, and how is it different from multimode?">Single mode fiber uses a narrow glass core carrying one light path, built for long distance runs between buildings, across a campus, or between cities, typically specified as OS2 (G.652D or bend insensitive G.657). Multimode fiber uses a wider core and multiple light paths, built for shorter runs inside a building or data center row, typically OM3 or OM4. We supply both, build-to-order on Fujikura preform glass.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="What is composite fiber optic cable?">Composite fiber optic cable, also sold as copper fiber composite cable, puts optical fibers and copper conductors in one sheath, so a single pull carries both data and power to a remote site such as a camera, radio or sensor. Vocom supplies composite fiber cable build-to-order, with a standard lead time of 6 to 8 weeks and up to 10 weeks for custom builds.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Can Vocom be a second source for distributors?">Yes. Rollable ribbon, high-count, micro and indoor plenum cable are the specs most often quoted in months elsewhere. Send the spec and we return a price and a delivery date. Any spec can be built to order as a custom build.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Can orders be split across ship dates?">Yes. Large orders are commonly split into tranches so cable arrives against your customers' build phases instead of sitting in your yard.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="Do you hold US stock?">No. Vocom is build-to-order with no US warehouse. Standard lead time is 6 to 8 weeks, expedited air freight is 2 to 3 weeks, and high-count or custom builds take up to 10 weeks.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xousmhh"><FaqItem question="I make duct or run a consultancy. Can I refer a customer?">Yes. Send the customer contact and what they are building, and we will quote it, build to order and deliver, with documentation and customs coordinated. HDPE microduct and vaults can be quoted alongside the cable.</FaqItem></div></div></div><div class="custom-fiber-cta xewiu4z fb"><p class="x07kli4">Need a Fiber Built to Your Exact Specification?</p><p class="xjvjuiw">Fiber count, jacket, rating and connector, we can source and build any fiber optic cable to match your spec.</p><a class="talk-to-a-specifier-button xlhk6xe" href="/contact-vocomai"><p class="x44fioc">Talk to a Specifier</p><svg class="xkmi4bm icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M 0 0 L 6.75 6.75 L 0 13.5 Z" fill-opacity="var(--icon-alpha, 0)" fill="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(13.5 5.25)"></path><path d="M 0 0 L 9.75 0" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(3.75 12)"></path><path d="M 0 0 L 6.75 6.75 L 0 13.5 Z" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(13.5 5.25)"></path></svg></a></div><section class="why-source-through-vocom xrathlz"><div class="why-introduction xgkzsa5"><h2 class="x6awgik">Why source it through Vocom</h2></div><div class="sourcing-reason-grid x2b1t0h"><div class="build-to-order xbxtb0n fb"><svg class="xfh04zm icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M 0 2.25 C 0 1.007 1.007 0 2.25 0 C 3.493 0 4.5 1.007 4.5 2.25 C 4.5 3.493 3.493 4.5 2.25 4.5 C 1.007 4.5 0 3.493 0 2.25 Z" fill-opacity="var(--icon-alpha, 0)" fill="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(7.5 5.25)"></path><path d="M 0 2.25 C 0 1.007 1.007 0 2.25 0 